course: dictionary
lesson: 7886
title: Random: chosen by chance
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Random means happening or chosen with no plan, pattern or reason, so you cannot guess it in advance. «A jury is twelve ordinary adults picked at random» means nobody picked them for a special reason. Any ordinary adult might have been chosen.
explain: Random can also be an informal word meaning strange or unexpected. «That was so random» means it was odd and did not fit with what was going on. Read the words around it to decide which meaning fits.
explain: Look for the phrase «at random», which means by chance. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it. If «chosen by chance» still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Random means chosen by chance, with no plan or pattern.
fact: «At random» means by chance, so every choice has an equal chance of being picked.
fact: In science, samples are chosen at random to make a test fair.
fact: Informal: «random» can mean strange or unexpected, as in «that was so random».
fact: A random person or thing is just any one, not a special or known one.
exercise: «A jury is twelve ordinary adults picked at random.» What does at random mean here? | Chosen in alphabetical order | Chosen because they are famous | *Chosen by chance, with no special reason | Chosen by the judge's friends
exercise: Ella says, «That was so random!» after a bird flew into the classroom. What does random mean here? | Very fast | *Strange and unexpected | Planned for weeks
exercise: In maths, what does picking a card at random mean? | *Every card has the same chance of being picked | You choose the card you like most | The best card is always picked | The card with the biggest number is picked
test: What is a good way to make a strong password that is easy to remember? | Use password123 | Use your name and your birthday | Use the word password | *Use a long password made of three random words joined together
test: «A rating is not random; it tells you what is inside.» Why is a rating not random? | It is chosen by chance | *It is based on a reason, so it is not picked by chance | It is a random number
exam: «Scams look like luck: "You've won a free phone!" when you entered no competition.» What should you do with a free game from a random site? | Click any links that come with it | Download it at once | *Get apps only from official stores and never click links
